% Obligation: x * 3 == x + (x << 1)
% The first obligation in the tree that uses `mul`. It is a real
% multiplier-vs-adder miter: mul(x,3) builds two partial-product rows and one
% 64-bit ripple-carry add, and the right-hand side reaches the same value
% through the shifter and the adder. Before `mul` existed, no .obl could state
% a multiplication at all (tools/certgen.py blast(): var/const/and/or/xor/not/
% add/shl/lshr/eq).
obligation mul_three_is_x_plus_shl1
1 var x
2 const 3
3 mul 1 2
4 shl 1 1
5 add 1 4
6 eq 3 5
prove 6
